Article 7 (Persons Eligible for Legal Aid)
(1) Persons eligible to receive legal aid from public-service legal officers under Article 33-3 of the Act shall be persons falling under any of the following subparagraphs:
1. Farmers and fishers;
2. Workers and small-scale merchants;
3. National and local public officials;
4. Persons entitled to veterans benefits;
5. Consumers who have suffered damage from the use of goods or services;
6. Petitioners in cases where the Constitutional Court has appointed a public-service legal officer as court-appointed counsel;
7. Suspects or defendants in cases where a court has appointed a public-service legal officer as court-appointed defense counsel;
8. Foreign nationals residing in the Republic of Korea;
9. Recipients of benefits under the National Basic Living Security Act;
10. Persons with disabilities or other citizens who face economic hardship and lack legal knowledge and are unable to secure legal remedies on their own.
(2) The specific scope of persons eligible for legal aid under the subparagraphs of paragraph (1) shall be determined by the internal regulations of a legal aid corporation, subject to approval by the Minister of Justice.
